{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions","id":1507403,"title":"[Tome of the Pentacle] Factions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-04T07:57:56-07:00","id":1507403,"title":"[Tome of the Pentacle] Factions","content":"Who wants a preview?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-factions/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-factions/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Tome of the Pentacle] Factions &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-factions/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/tome-of-the-pentacle-factions/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T08:03:07-07:00","id":1507405,"title":"","content":"Amazing! I like the Council of Dragons!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T08:36:50-07:00","id":1507411,"title":"","content":"I love how smoothly this builds on the foundations of the 1ed Order book and <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, it just makes me more excited for the release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-04-2023, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T12:54:24-07:00","id":1507435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions#post1507403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants a preview?</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"200\" height=\"112\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/powerpuff/images/5/56/Tumblr_inline_mpls00b4cb1qz4rgp.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/powerpuff/images/5/56/Tumblr_inline_mpls00b4cb1qz4rgp.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/powerpuff/images/5/56/Tumblr_inline_mpls00b4cb1qz4rgp.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#ffffff\">Ridiculous requirement</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T12:57:25-07:00","id":1507436,"title":"","content":"That was pretty neat. I hope we get another quick bite to really wet our appetites!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T17:16:40-07:00","id":1507441,"title":"","content":"I like this as a middle ground between Order and Legacy and it's potential for diverse political conflicts as you get into arguments about who is putting the wrong emPHAsis on THE wrong teNET.<br /> <br /> I also love that the Crucible are <i>those</i> messy bitches who live for the drama (so to speak).<br /> <br /> On the vote for next time, guys, we have the Tremere in Nameless and Accursed, and while I am curious how they looked in their time in the Diamond, I'd rather get more on one of the two Mysterium predecessors. THere's new weirdness to be had!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2023, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T21:40:05-07:00","id":1507454,"title":"","content":"Speculation! It's entirely possible that there are more Arrow factions in the book, but the Black Tower is the only one from 1e that we didn't see here. Have they become the &quot;generic&quot; Arrow faction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T01:58:26-07:00","id":1507463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions?p=1507441#post1507441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and while I am curious how they looked in their time in the Diamond...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's probably it. I had visions of a 4th redo of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T06:29:58-07:00","id":1507476,"title":"","content":"It's not a redo of the Hollow Tremere from 1e/Left Hand Path/Nameless and Accursed - it's the Order that they were a secret society *inside*. Think of it as having had the Tal'mah'ra for the entire run of yhe gameline and only now getting the Sabbat splat pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T09:59:24-07:00","id":1507491,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I feel as though this doesn't quite cover what I would imagine from the term &quot;faction&quot;. I would think factions in an Order would constitute incompatible agendas that compete for primacy, where these are more like schools of thought.<br /> <br /> Expansion of tool yantras is an interesting way to make that showcase itself a bit more, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T10:06:02-07:00","id":1507492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions?p=1507491#post1507491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I feel as though this doesn't quite cover what I would imagine from the term &quot;faction&quot;. I would think factions in an Order would constitute incompatible agendas that compete for primacy, where these are more like schools of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of thing did you have in mind? To me, these seem about as detailed you reasonably can get on a global level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T22:08:57-07:00","id":1507549,"title":"","content":"Good stuff. I'm actually most curious about the Divine Spear, since they're not expounded on, but I suppose I'll have to wait for the book.<br /> <br /> I think they work fine as factions, though the word &quot;ideology&quot; might be better suited. They're most like templates for NPCs or explanations for implied alliances, which is always welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T01:28:36-07:00","id":1507563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions?p=1507492#post1507492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of thing did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not necessarily saying that I want factions in the manner that I've described, just that it's what I'd expect from using the term.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I'd feel as though divisions in the Adamantine Arrow that would constitute factions would be things like whether they should be purely defensive for their cabals and Consilia, whether they should continuously and actively be engaged in campaigns of aggression against enemies of the Awakened (which can itself splinter into a few factions of differing opinion about what the enemies of the Awakened should be), and whether or not the creed of the Arrows should extend to protecting the Sleepers (with its own divisions of &quot;do we only defend them from the supernatural, or from anything that is bad). Maybe even a faction of those who feel the rebranding of the Order has not worked out (or was never the right call) and they should go back to participating in Sleeper wars.<br /> <br /> I feel as though it's a term that lends itself to scenarios of tension and intrigue in which one faction tries to hijack things to set the course for the whole group. This faction pulled off some scheme and now everybody feels like it's necessary to go along with the pro-active operations against the Seers even if their hearts aren't in it. I wouldn't see that kind of competition between, say, the Ashen and most of the others. There's too much capacity for live and let live in these for me to really view them as factions.<br /> <br /> Still, as far as the point about what can work on a global level goes, that would also be why I would think an Order would typically be factionalised more on the caucus level and more often in response to local conditions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T02:55:56-07:00","id":1507567,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> raises good points.<br /> <br /> Another thing not working with those <b>Factions as in blog post is Order Status 2 requirement</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a bit bonkers in my POV. On general, beside <i><b>Vedanti</b></i>, they are all sub-philosophies of particular Order - and even Vidanti is pointed to be more as 'ex-Arrow retirement plan' than something really transformative.<br /> <br /> From what I read in blog post they could easily be used by characters from start, just after intial Order training. Order Status 2 are often characters that are responsible on important task around local caucus levels. Fresh characters can work even with Order Status 0 ( zero ), as pointed time and time again in books of <b>MtAw</b> gameline.<br /> <br /> Needing Order Status 2 seems counterintuitive to 'generalize' feel those inner-Order factions have. \ud83d\ude10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T12:07:26-07:00","id":1507595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions?p=1507567#post1507567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> raises good points.<br /> <br /> Another thing not working with those <b>Factions as in blog post is Order Status 2 requirement</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a bit bonkers in my POV. On general, beside <i><b>Vedanti</b></i>, they are all sub-philosophies of particular Order - and even Vidanti is pointed to be more as 'ex-Arrow retirement plan' than something really transformative.<br /> <br /> From what I read in blog post they could easily be used by characters from start, just after intial Order training. Order Status 2 are often characters that are responsible on important task around local caucus levels. Fresh characters can work even with Order Status 0 ( zero ), as pointed time and time again in books of <b>MtAw</b> gameline.<br /> <br /> Needing Order Status 2 seems counterintuitive to 'generalize' feel those inner-Order factions have. \ud83d\ude10</div> </div> </div> </div>You could bean aspiring member (in training) of those sub-factions before actually buying the faction merit...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T12:54:49-07:00","id":1507597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507403-tome-of-the-pentacle-factions?p=1507567#post1507567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> raises good points.<br /> <br /> Another thing not working with those <b>Factions as in blog post is Order Status 2 requirement</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a bit bonkers in my POV. On general, beside <i><b>Vedanti</b></i>, they are all sub-philosophies of particular Order - and even Vidanti is pointed to be more as 'ex-Arrow retirement plan' than something really transformative.<br /> <br /> From what I read in blog post they could easily be used by characters from start, just after intial Order training. Order Status 2 are often characters that are responsible on important task around local caucus levels. Fresh characters can work even with Order Status 0 ( zero ), as pointed time and time again in books of <b>MtAw</b> gameline.<br /> <br /> Needing Order Status 2 seems counterintuitive to 'generalize' feel those inner-Order factions have. \ud83d\ude10</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you positing that specialized blocs that build on a sound understanding and demonstration of an Order's principle's and dedication to a particular take on that Order's roles should be available to people who just barely proved their value and are likely to flipflop on their position because they're still getting their feet?<br /> <br /> Because a) THis is the sort compartmentalization and specialization that happens in any organization, and it's reflective of the fact that you often need to prove yourself competent and reliable as an agent (not a trainee, an agent of the organization) before you get this particular set of responsibilities and training,<br /> b) players who aren't set on a faction to begin with probably could do with time to see how their characters actually play, and setting the bar 2 dots high let's them take them time while being minimal enough the one's ready out of the gate can just start off with it,<br /> but also c) Order Status 2 is such a small bump in the road that if you personally want to avoid it, you can just waive it and I don't think anyone will blink.<br /> <br /> Or is this another &quot;I don't want there to be any impediment to a new toy I want to play with in my group, and I don't want the book to disagree with me&quot; thing, ala <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1095950-2e-hack-sacred-hunt-for-everyone\">Sacred Hunt</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209600-hack-bpg-obcasus-rites-for-free\">Obcasus Initiate</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1196390-mage-2e-signs-of-sorcery-problem-no-sharing-paths-mage-sight-between-cabal\">Aedes</a>? Because if it's that, I'd like to know now so I can check out of this part of the conversation early and otherwise let you do you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, the Vidanti are illustrative for the Order requirement argument: why would the Arrow have a tolerant appreciation of some scrub who barely amounted to the recognition comparable to an E-2 Private in the US Army suddenly losing their stomach for violence and turning to a life of pacifism? You need to have proven you a) actually committed to the philosophy of violence enough to prove you really understood it and tried living it, b) have demonstrated enough skill and understanding to make you a possibly viable asset as a sorcerous mentor, and c) have been through some actual shit where the trauma you're living with is understandable enough to support an venerable (if dishonorable) discharge. An Order Status 1 Arrow, a Talon retiring, isn't an asset to be valued as much as mourned, that's just a fucking coward who probably shouldn't have picked up the sword to begin with, as far as the Arrow is concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-06-2023, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}